{
  "facts": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "at": null,
      "u": 0,
      "text": "Welcome to the reef. Coral reefs cover less than 1% of the ocean floor, but about a quarter of all ocean species live on them."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "at": [
        -14,
        -12,
        1
      ],
      "look": "anemone",
      "text": "Clownfish live among sea anemones. A slimy coating keeps the anemone’s sting from hurting them."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "at": [
        -5,
        -10,
        8.5
      ],
      "look": "turtle",
      "text": "A sea turtle! Sea turtles have swum in the oceans for more than 100 million years."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "at": [
        6,
        -10.5,
        -1.5
      ],
      "text": "You’re in a kelp forest. Giant kelp can grow about 60 cm (2 feet) in a single day."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "at": [
        21,
        -10,
        2.4
      ],
      "look": "school",
      "text": "Fish swim in schools to stay safe. In a big group, it’s hard for a hunter to catch any one fish."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "at": [
        25.8,
        -9,
        9.6
      ],
      "look": "shark",
      "text": "Look down! Whale sharks are the biggest fish in the sea, and they eat tiny plankton."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "at": [
        28,
        -7,
        17.5
      ],
      "look": "manta",
      "text": "Manta rays glide by flapping their wide fins like wings."
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "at": [
        21,
        -5,
        25.6
      ],
      "look": "jelly",
      "text": "Jellyfish have no brain, no heart and no bones."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "at": null,
      "u": 0.93,
      "text": "This reef is made up for the campus, inspired by ocean VR like Hydrous, a partner listed by XRLibraries. Read “Oceans in VR” in the library."
    }
  ],
